# board.pdl - {{Title}}: the track, as DATA (the STUB step function of the shared engine game_core: every tick x += direction, first to the end of the track wins; a real game replaces the step function). The first ledger row records the hash of this file and rules.pdl:
# editing either after a game began makes every verb refuse that ledger (start a new game).
# TRACK | length | N           squares 1..N; everybody starts on 0; reaching N or more wins
# JUMP  | from | to | label     landing on `from` moves you to `to` (a ladder goes up, a chute goes down; one jump per landing, no chains). Chutes and Ladders is exactly these rows.
TRACK | length | 30
# JUMP | 4  | 14 | ladder
# JUMP | 17 | 6  | chute
